Prefix ext/intl MessageFormatAdapter methods with php, the way php-src itself
does from 7.4 on, so a statically-linked ICU does not collide with them.

ext/intl/msgformat/msgformat_helpers.cpp opens U_NAMESPACE_BEGIN and defines
icu::MessageFormatAdapter::getArgTypeList() -- ICU declares that class a friend
of MessageFormat, and php-src reuses it as a backdoor to a private method. ICU
defines the very same symbol in its own umsg.cpp. Against a shared libicui18n
that never matters: the definition lives inside the .so and the linker never
sees a second one. deps/build-deps.sh builds ICU --enable-static
--disable-shared on purpose (no duplicate 30 MB ICU data blob in the image, and
nothing else in it can dlopen an EOL ICU), so the linker does pull umsg.ao in
and reports

  multiple definition of icu_67::MessageFormatAdapter::getArgTypeList(
  icu_67::MessageFormat const&, int&)

at the final link of sapi/cli/php -- after the whole tree has compiled, in a
file whose name gives no hint that the cause is a linkage choice made in
deps/build-deps.sh.

php-src fixed this in 7.4 by renaming its own methods to phpGetArgTypeList and
phpGetMessagePattern, with the comment "Prefix the methods with php to avoid
clashes with any definitions in ICU." This is that rename, applied to the same
call sites. The one occurrence deliberately left alone is

  return m.getArgTypeList(count);

which is ICU own real private method being called, not the php-src wrapper.

7.4 and 8.0 carry the rename upstream and need no patch. 7.0, 7.1, 7.2
and 7.3 all need it; the php-7.1 and php-7.2 copies are byte-identical, and the
7.0 and 7.3 ones differ from them only in hunk line numbers (see
deps/patches/README.md).

--- a/ext/intl/msgformat/msgformat_helpers.cpp
+++ b/ext/intl/msgformat/msgformat_helpers.cpp
@@ -57,22 +57,22 @@
